title: Point the way off the screen
intro: An Edge Pointer is an objective marker: an arrow on the screen's edge showing which way to look for something out of view, sliding along the edge as the camera moves, gone once it's in view, and a click away from gliding the camera there.

project: Empty | Edge Pointer

chapter: A floor, a worker far off, and a camera | Camera Controls on the camera
create: Tilemap
rename: Level
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n222211112222111122221111222211112222\n111122221111222211112222111122221111\n111122221111222211112222111122221111
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Worker
set: Transform.Position = 2, -9, 0
say: The worker stands at the far left of the floor.
deselect
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position = 30, -9, -10
set: Camera.Size = 6
set: Camera.HudSize = 6
add: CameraControls
pick: CameraControls.StayInside = Level
say: The camera starts over on the right, where the player can pan and zoom it.

chapter: The pointer | Entity, UI, Edge Pointer
deselect
create: Edge Pointer
pick: EdgePointer.Target = Worker
explain: field:EdgePointer.Target | Target | Its Target is what it points at. A trigger, a button or a script moves it on to the next goal as the game goes.
explain: field:EdgePointer.Margin | Margin | Margin is how far in from the screen's edges it sits. It keeps its size on the screen as the camera zooms, like the rest of the HUD.
explain: field:EdgePointer.InView | In View | While the worker is in view it hides. Over Target would sit it over the worker instead, pointing down, so one arrow marks it on the screen and off it.
explain: field:Button.Do | Do | Its button's Do is Glide: a click glides the camera to the worker. The text inside it shows how far off the worker is.

chapter: Play | It points, slides, hides and glides
play
wait: 1
expectvalue: Edge Pointer.EdgePointer.IsOnEdge = true
say: The worker is off to the left, so the arrow sits on the left edge, pointing at it, with the distance beside it.
hold: Up 1
say: Pan up and it slides down the edge, staying on the line to the worker.
hold: Left 2.5
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Edge Pointer.EdgePointer.IsOnEdge = false
say: With the worker in view, the arrow's gone.
hold: Right 2.5
wait: 0.5
expectvalue: Edge Pointer.EdgePointer.IsOnEdge = true
say: Pan away and it's back.
gameclick: Edge Pointer
wait: 1.5
expectvalue: Main Camera.CameraControls.IsFocused = false
expectvalue: Edge Pointer.EdgePointer.IsOnEdge = false
say: A click on it glides the camera over to the worker and hands it straight back to the player.
stop
